Subject: stb_image_resize: no loop vectorization with GCC on AltiVec without VSX

GCC 16.2 at -O3 with -mcpu=cell (also -mcpu=970, -mcpu=power6 -maltivec; not plain -O3, not -O2)
vectorizes the 4-channel loop of stbir__resample_horizontal_downsample wrongly. Every downscale
comes out nearly black and transparent: all generated mipmap levels (level 1 of a 1024x1024 RGBA
page sums to 465002 instead of 103538663) and every image the texturesize option scales down.
The 3D view's textures sample those levels, and the models' alpha test discards them, so on the
PS3 the terrain was black and the structures invisible while the HUD (no mipmaps) was right.
-DNDEBUG is part of the trigger (the asserts in the loop stop the vectorizer). Turn off loop
vectorization for this file only on such targets; the SLP vectorizer and -O3 otherwise stay.

---
diff --git a/lib/ivis_opengl/3rdparty/stb_image_resize.cpp b/lib/ivis_opengl/3rdparty/stb_image_resize.cpp
--- a/lib/ivis_opengl/3rdparty/stb_image_resize.cpp
+++ b/lib/ivis_opengl/3rdparty/stb_image_resize.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,13 @@
 #  pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wfloat-conversion"
 #endif
 
+// GCC 16 with AltiVec and no VSX (-mcpu=cell, also 970 / power6 -maltivec) at -O3 vectorizes the 4-channel
+// horizontal downsampling loop of stbir__resample_horizontal_downsample wrongly: every mipmap level and
+// every downscaled image comes out nearly black and transparent (textures of the 3D view on the PS3)
+#if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__) && defined(__ALTIVEC__) && !defined(__VSX__)
+#  pragma GCC optimize("no-tree-loop-vectorize")
+#endif
+
 #define STB_IMAGE_RESIZE_IMPLEMENTATION
 #include "stb_image_resize.h"
 
